From dd54bc7b4a2294095a20b6e71b3f56a2a49af0d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:51:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Sun shadows: the palms shaded and lit as Wind Waker HD's

DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_SKINNED_SCENERY=1: only the toon-shaded draws (the mask's green 1: Link, the
islanders) are characters to the sun pass; skinned-only ones (green 0.6: a palm's swaying leaves) are
scenery, as HD lights Outset's palms with its scenery's shader: they take the facing term, terrain mix and
the scenery's caster bias and lookup (with the characters' their thin leaves shaded themselves), and smooth
normals made on the CPU like solid scenery's, drawn by the mask's pass (kind 9: a cut-out part with its
normal). A leaf is lit from either side (the mask turns a normal to the side seen; HD's leaf normals point off
the frond's top whichever side is seen); without normals of its own and none made, no facing term.

DOL_AURORA_HD_VERTEX_COLOURS: a table of HD's vertex colours by the same exact positions ('BWHC': x, y, z, r,
g, b, a). A draw that takes smooth normals and mixes its shade colour (C0) to its light colour by its vertex
colour (first stage lerp(C0, KONST, RASC) from colour channel 0; no later stage reads C0) takes HD's light:
C0 black and HD's colour as its vertex colour, so it gives texture x HD's colour x the light colour and the
sun pass makes the light (a position the table lacks keeps its own result). Its in-between frames take the
same constants.

DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_SMOOTH_AMBIENT=1: skinned scenery's ambient mixed from sky to ground by its smooth
normal, as HD's per-vertex light is, not by the depth's normal of a cut-out leaf card.
